</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Doctoral Course Sequence</h1>

    <h2>Research Foundation (12 - 15 Credits)</h2>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>STA 7114 Advanced Statistics</li>
        <li>EDA 6415 Intro to Qualitative Inquiry</li>
        <li>EDA 7416 Advanced Qualitative Inquiry</li>
        <li>EDA 7912 Advanced Research (Literature Review)</li>
        <li>EDF 7482 Advanced Educational Research (Research Proposal)</li>
        <li>EME 6426 Administrative Applications of Educational Technology*</li>
    </ul>
    <p><small>*Waiver with on-line learning modules/assessment</small></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Doctoral Course Sequence</h1>

    <h2>Comprehensive Examination</h2>
    <p>After 2/3 of the coursework (around 40 credit hours), students will sit for a comprehensive examination which focuses on general knowledge of leadership plus specific knowledge of K-12 leadership.</p>
    <p>After passing the comprehensive examination, students will commence the process of declaring candidacy and completing their dissertations.</p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Doctoral Course Sequence</h1>

    <h2>Dissertation (20 Credits)</h2>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>Select Dissertation Chair/Committee</li>
        <li>Prepare a concept paper</li>
        <li>Admission to Candidacy</li>
        <li>Development of Proposal & Proposal Hearing</li>
        <li>Institutional Review Board (IRB) Approval</li>
        <li>Conduct Research</li>
        <li>Defend Dissertation</li>
        <li>GRADUATE!</li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Possible Delivery Options</h1>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>Executive Track Classes – Six Saturdays, 8:30 to 4:30, two courses per semester during Fall and Spring</li>
        <li>Evening Classes - 1 night per week for the entire semester (16 weeks)</li>
        <li>Online Classes* – fully delivered over the web using Blackboard</li>
    </ul>
    <p><small>*Doctoral foundation courses are offered exclusively f2f on campus.</small></p>
    <p><small>-See course Schedule for executive track dates.</small></p>
    <p><small>-Doctoral program is Boca based. Cohorts are occasionally formed on other campuses.</small></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>General Admission Requirements:</h1>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>Minimum graduate GPA 3.0</li>
        <li>Competitive GRE score</li>
        <li><small>* (GRE results are required for a complete application, regardless of score)</small></li>
        <li><p><strong>Note:</strong> Meeting the minimum admission requirements does not guarantee admission to the program</p></li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>The Graduate Record Exam (GRE)</h1>
    <p>GRE testing is computer based.</p>
    <p>To register for the verbal & quantitative parts go to: <a href="http://www.gre.org">http://www.gre.org</a></p>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Application Process Part I</h1>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>Complete the graduate admissions application on-line (found at: <a href="http://www.fau.edu/graduate/applynow.php">http://www.fau.edu/graduate/applynow.php</a>)</li>
        <li>Obtain official copies of all post-secondary transcripts.</li>
        <li>Submit these and GRE scores to:
            <p>Florida Atlantic University</p>
            <p>Graduate College</p>
            <p>SU 80, RM. 101</p>
            <p>777 Glades Road, P.O. Box 3091</p>
            <p>Boca Raton, FL 33431-0991</p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <h1>Application Process Part II</h1>
    <p>Complete and submit the following to the <span data-field="department.name">{{ department.name }}</span></p>
    <ul class="course-list">
        <li>An essay that identifies your career goals and how the program you are seeking admittance into will enable you to meet these goals</li>
        <li>A professional <span data-field="document_type">{{ document_type }}</span></li>
        <li>3 letters of professional <span data-field="reference_type">{{ reference_type }}</span> (one should be from a professor)</li>
        <li>Your current <span data-field="email_address">{{ email_address }}</span> address</li>
        <li><strong>Submit materials to:</strong>
            <p>Florida Atlantic University</p>
            <p>The Department of Educational Leadership and Research Methodology</p>
            <p>College of Education-Suite 240</p>
            <p>777 Glades Road,</p>
            <p>Boca Raton, FL 33431-0991</p>
            <p>Attn: Ph.D. School Leadership Application Materials</p>
        </li>
    </ul>
</div>

</body>
</html>

